<main class="commercial" id="main-content"><div class="wrap">
<section class="px-hero" aria-labelledby="px-title" data-product-home="2"><div class="px-copy"><p class="px-kicker">CRANIO SYSTEMS / Head &amp; Neck Optimization</p><h1 id="px-title">A freer neck.<br>A clearer head.</h1><p class="px-lead">Explore the relationship between head position, everyday experience and directions for individual development.</p><p class="px-zero">Zero is not the goal.</p><div class="px-actions"><a class="px-primary" href="#px-roles">Explore your possibilities</a><a class="px-secondary" href="en/start/">Discuss your situation</a></div></div><div class="px-instrument"><p class="px-kicker">01 / Configuration / illustrative model</p><fieldset class="px-config"><legend>Illustrative head orientation</legend><input type="radio" name="px-orientation" id="px-left"><label for="px-left">Left</label><input type="radio" name="px-orientation" id="px-center" checked><label for="px-center">Centre</label><input type="radio" name="px-orientation" id="px-right"><label for="px-right">Right</label><svg class="px-diagram" viewBox="0 0 400 340" role="img" aria-label="C0–C1"><g fill="none" stroke="currentColor" opacity=".22"><circle cx="200" cy="154" r="130"/><circle cx="200" cy="154" r="108"/><path d="M200 15V318M32 210H368" stroke-dasharray="3 7"/></g><g fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" opacity=".7"><path d="M93 324Q127 275 167 260L181 212H219L233 260Q273 275 307 324"/><path d="M181 225h38m-41 13h44m-48 13h52m-57 13h62"/></g><g class="px-head" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.6" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M200 35C135 35 113 82 114 125L126 161Q140 181 169 193L182 210H218L231 193Q260 181 274 161L286 125C287 82 265 35 200 35Z"/><path d="M130 124Q154 106 181 124M219 124Q246 106 270 124M200 116V156L186 161M173 178Q200 188 227 178" opacity=".72"/><path d="M200 41V207M122 125H278" stroke-dasharray="4 5" opacity=".56"/></g><circle cx="200" cy="210" r="8" fill="var(--px-accent)"/><circle cx="200" cy="210" r="16" fill="none" stroke="var(--px-accent)"/><text x="223" y="207" fill="var(--px-accent)" font-size="12">C0–C1</text></svg></fieldset><p class="px-note">A schematic illustration, not an assessment of your anatomy or a target angle.</p><details><summary>What does this model show?</summary><p>It illustrates one component of head orientation relative to the neck. Individual configuration requires observation and assessment.</p><a href="en/c0-c1/">C0–C1 ↗</a></details></div></section>
<section class="px-section" id="px-roles"><p class="px-kicker">02 / Recognition · Role-based depth</p><h2>Start with your own context.</h2><p class="px-lead">Choose a route. Explore what is relevant to you without an obligatory questionnaire.</p><div class="px-role-grid"><details><summary>For myself</summary><p>Recognize familiar experiences and learn how a first visit works.</p><a href="en/experience/">Explore ↗</a></details><details><summary>Business owner · RU</summary><p>Consider individual and organizational context.</p><a href="ru/professions/for-companies/">Explore ↗</a></details><details><summary>Professional · RU</summary><p>Explore the demands of your working day.</p><a href="ru/professions/">Explore ↗</a></details><details><summary>Future specialist</summary><p>Discover the learning architecture.</p><a href="en/education/">Explore ↗</a></details><details><summary>Corporate client · RU</summary><p>Discuss a program for your team.</p><a href="ru/professions/for-companies/">Explore ↗</a></details><details><summary>Researcher</summary><p>Explore the research framework and cranial reference.</p><a href="en/primordocciput/">Explore ↗</a></details><details><summary>Technology partner</summary><p>Explore the Vita Wellness demonstration.</p><a href="technology/vita-wellness/">Explore ↗</a></details><details><summary>International partner</summary><p>Discuss cooperation and technology.</p><a href="en/technology/">Explore ↗</a></details></div></section>
<section class="px-section" id="px-potential"><p class="px-kicker">03 / Potential</p><h2>Explore directions of potential.</h2><div class="px-axis-grid"><details><summary>Physical</summary><p>Comfort, movement and perceived effort.</p></details><details><summary>Cognitive</summary><p>Attention, mental workload and perceived fatigue.</p></details><details><summary>Emotional</summary><p>Everyday experiences of tension and ease.</p></details><details><summary>Professional</summary><p>Working conditions, tasks and recovery.</p></details></div><p class="px-note">These are directions for observation, not predictions of individual outcomes.</p><a class="px-primary" href="en/start/">Discuss your situation</a></section>
<section class="px-section" id="px-products"><p class="px-kicker">04 / Product architecture</p><h2>One system. Ten ways to explore.</h2><div class="px-product-grid"><article><span class="px-state">Existing RU entry</span><h3>Personal Navigator</h3><p>Self-recognition and observation</p><a href="ru/recognition/">Explore ↗</a></article><article><span class="px-state">Illustration</span><h3>Configuration</h3><p>Head and neck orientation</p><a href="#px-title">Explore ↗</a></article><article><span class="px-state">Concept</span><h3>Potential</h3><p>Directions for individual development</p><a href="#px-potential">Explore ↗</a></article><article><span class="px-state">RU routes</span><h3>Professional</h3><p>Role-specific working demands</p><a href="ru/professions/">Explore ↗</a></article><article><span class="px-state">Section</span><h3>Cases</h3><p>Individual observations and records</p><a href="en/cases/">Explore ↗</a></article><article><span class="px-state">Information</span><h3>Academy</h3><p>Learning and competence</p><a href="en/education/">Explore ↗</a></article><article><span class="px-state">Interactive project</span><h3>Technology</h3><p>Vita Wellness interactive project</p><a href="technology/vita-wellness/">Explore ↗</a></article><article><span class="px-state">Inquiry</span><h3>Corporate</h3><p>Programs for owners and teams</p><a href="ru/professions/for-companies/">Explore ↗</a></article><article><span class="px-state">Research</span><h3>Research</h3><p>C0–C1 and Primordocciput</p><a href="en/primordocciput/">Explore ↗</a></article><article><span class="px-state">Concept</span><h3>TwinMind</h3><p>Continuity of observation; no connected account</p><a href="en/twinmind/">Explore ↗</a></article></div></section>
<div class="px-prior"><p class="px-kicker">05 / Practice · Observation</p><h2>Practical information and existing observations</h2></div>

<section class="px-legacy-hero" aria-labelledby="cr-headline"><div class="cr-hero-copy"><p class="cr-kicker">CRANIO · Head & Neck · Kyrgyzstan</p><h2 id="cr-headline">Persistent neck tension?</h2><p class="cr-lead">CRANIO provides percussion-assisted soft-tissue sessions for the upper neck and occipital muscles. We compare comfort and movement before and after. This is not medical treatment.</p><div class="cr-actions"><a class="cr-button cr-primary" href="/en/start/" data-booking="contact">Contact by email</a><a class="cr-button cr-outline" href="#session">How a session works</a></div><p class="cr-small">This practice is not medical diagnosis or treatment. Individual outcomes vary and are not guaranteed.</p></div><aside class="cr-process" aria-label="What happens at an appointment"><p class="cr-kicker">01 / 04</p><h2>What happens at an appointment</h2><ol><li>Discuss your concern and relevant limitations</li><li>Check movement, sensations and observable reference points</li><li>Work with soft tissues in the head and neck region</li><li>Compare observations afterward and discuss next steps</li></ol><p class="cr-small">You do not need to buy a device; the practitioner uses the instrument during the session.</p></aside></section>
<section class="cr-section" id="recognition-entry"><p class="cr-kicker">Self-recognition · Russian-language checklist</p><h2>Do these experiences sound familiar?</h2><p class="cr-intro">Select familiar everyday experiences, generate your own list, and request a consultation. The interactive checklist is currently available in Russian.</p><div class="cr-actions"><a class="cr-button cr-primary" href="ru/recognition/">Open self-recognition checklist (RU) →</a><a class="cr-button cr-outline" href="ru/specializations/">20 practice modules (RU) →</a></div></section>
<section class="cr-section" id="professional-recognition"><p class="cr-kicker">CRANIO · Professional recognition · VRL v1.0</p><h2>See how your working day involves your head and neck</h2><p class="cr-intro">Role-specific Russian-language pages for software developers, AI/ML specialists, designers and video editors. Recognize familiar situations and request an individual or workplace conversation.</p><div class="cr-actions"><a class="cr-button cr-primary" href="ru/professions/">Explore professions (RU) →</a><a class="cr-button cr-outline" href="ru/recognition/">Recognition map (RU)</a></div></section>
<section class="cr-section" id="concerns"><p class="cr-kicker">Start with what feels familiar</p><h2>Reasons people contact us</h2><p class="cr-intro">The same symptom can have different causes. Head position alone cannot establish a diagnosis, and we do not promise to resolve every problem.</p><div class="cr-concerns"><a class="cr-concern" href="en/experience/neck-tension/"><span>01</span>Persistent neck tension<span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a class="cr-concern" href="en/experience/neck-stiffness/"><span>02</span>Neck stiffness and limited motion<span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a class="cr-concern" href="en/experience/screen-work/"><span>03</span>Screen-related fatigue<span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a class="cr-concern" href="en/experience/head-tension/"><span>04</span>Tension around the back of the head<span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a class="cr-concern" href="en/experience/facial-asymmetry/"><span>05</span>Facial and jaw asymmetry<span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a class="cr-concern" href="en/experience/comfortable-head/"><span>06</span>Difficulty finding a comfortable head position<span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></section>
<section class="cr-section" id="session"><p class="cr-kicker">A practical explanation</p><h2>What to expect at a first visit</h2><p class="cr-intro">We start with conversation and observation, then practical work if there is no reason to recommend medical assessment or to avoid the session.</p><div class="cr-steps"><div class="cr-card"><h3>01 · Conversation</h3><p>What you notice, how long it has been present, relevant assessments and warning signs.</p></div><div class="cr-card"><h3>02 · Initial observations</h3><p>Comfort, movement and — with consent — standardized photographs, when appropriate.</p></div><div class="cr-card"><h3>03 · Practical session</h3><p>A practitioner applies percussion-assisted soft-tissue work to the upper neck and occipital muscles, adjusting intensity to the individual.</p></div><div class="cr-card"><h3>04 · Reassessment</h3><p>We compare observations, including when nothing changes, and consider whether further visits make sense.</p></div></div><div class="cr-actions"><a class="cr-button cr-outline" href="en/how-it-works/">How a session works ↗</a></div></section>
<section class="cr-section" id="results"><p class="cr-kicker">Observations, not promises</p><h2>What we pay attention to</h2><p class="cr-intro">The practitioner has reported individual changes in perceived neck tension, freedom of movement and visible symmetry. These reports do not establish treatment efficacy.</p><div class="cr-three"><div class="cr-card"><h3>Movement</h3><p>Turning and tilting the head; any limitation and sense of effort.</p></div><div class="cr-card"><h3>Experience</h3><p>Perceived tension, head comfort and how you feel before and after.</p></div><div class="cr-card"><h3>Symmetry</h3><p>Comparable photos, with informed consent, consistent angle and lighting.</p></div></div><div class="cr-actions"><a class="cr-button cr-outline" href="en/cases/">How case records are documented ↗</a></div></section>
<section class="cr-section cr-split" id="model"><div><p class="cr-kicker">The C0–C1 model</p><h2>Why the occipital region matters in this approach</h2></div><div><p>C0 refers to the occipital bone, and C1 to the first cervical vertebra (atlas). CRANIO explores a hypothesis that relative skull position and muscular adaptation in this region could contribute to some movement and postural compensation patterns.</p><p class="cr-small cr-hypothesis">This is a research hypothesis, not an established explanation for all asymmetry, headaches or other conditions. External observation cannot establish bone displacement.</p><a class="cr-text-link" href="en/c0-c1/">Explore the C0–C1 model ↗</a></div></section>
<section class="cr-section" id="pricing"><p class="cr-kicker">Clear terms before you visit</p><h2>Sessions and indicative fees</h2><p class="cr-intro">Indicative prices from the previously defined Kyrgyzstan program. Please confirm current fees, location and availability in WhatsApp.</p><div class="cr-prices"><div><span>Initial session</span><strong>15 000 <small>KGS</small></strong></div><div><span>Follow-up session</span><strong>8 000 <small>KGS</small></strong></div><div><span>Three-session program</span><strong>31 000 <small>KGS</small></strong></div></div><p class="cr-small">Further sessions are not mandatory; their relevance is discussed after the first visit. Payments and terms are agreed directly with the practitioner.</p></section>
<section class="cr-section cr-split" id="author"><div><p class="cr-kicker">CRANIO SYSTEMS</p><h2>Who is behind CRANIO</h2></div><div><p>CRANIO SYSTEMS is an author-developed practical approach and research model by Lian Axis, informed by years of personal observations of head and neck work. Describing this experience is not a clinical efficacy claim.</p><a class="cr-text-link" href="en/method/">Read about the method ↗</a></div></section>
<section class="cr-section cr-safety" id="safety" role="note"><div><h2>When to seek medical care first</h2><p>Sudden severe headache, numbness or weakness, speech or vision changes, or pain after a head or neck injury require urgent medical assessment. Do not substitute a nonmedical session for necessary care.</p></div><p class="cr-small">CRANIO is a nonmedical soft-tissue practice and self-observation framework, not diagnosis or treatment.</p></section>
<section class="cr-section"><h2>Quick answers</h2><div class="cr-faq"><details><summary>Do I need to buy a device?</summary><p>No. The practitioner uses the percussion tool during a session.</p></details><details><summary>Will my atlas be adjusted?</summary><p>No cervical manipulation or vertebral adjustment is claimed. Work focuses on soft tissue, and external observation alone cannot verify bone alignment.</p></details><details><summary>Will one session fix the problem?</summary><p>No results are guaranteed. We document what changes and what does not. Discuss medical symptoms with a clinician.</p></details><details><summary>What is TwinMind?</summary><p>An optional concept for continuity of observation records. No app or account is required for a session.</p></details></div></section>
<section class="cr-finale" id="contact"><p class="cr-kicker">CRANIO SYSTEMS</p><h2>Tell us what is bothering you</h2><p>Message us about your head or neck concern and ask about appointment format, location and available times.</p><div class="cr-actions"><a class="cr-button cr-primary" href="/en/start/" data-booking="contact">Ask about an appointment</a><a class="cr-button cr-outline" href="en/primordocciput/">Research and development history ↗</a></div></section></div></main>